  "notes": "{祝|いわ}う is a godan verb meaning to celebrate an occasion or congratulate someone on an achievement.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pattern: ～⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{祝|いわ}う (to celebrate something)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{誕生日|たんじょうび}→誕生日：02910_tanjoubi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{祝|いわ}う: to celebrate a birthday\n- ⟦{結婚|けっこん}→結婚：02514_kekkon⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{祝|いわ}う: to celebrate a marriage\n- ⟦{合格|ごうかく}→合格：02816_goukaku⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{祝|いわ}う: to celebrate passing an exam\n- ⟦{成功|せいこう}→成功：02638_seikou⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{祝|いわ}う: to celebrate a success\n- ⟦{新年|しんねん}→新年：09787_shinnen⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{祝|いわ}う: to celebrate the new year\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦お{祝|いわ}い→お祝い：01339_oiwai⟧: celebration; congratulatory gift (noun form with honorific お)\n- ⟦{祝日|しゅくじつ}→祝日：07588_shukujitsu⟧: national holiday\n- ⟦{祝|しゅく}{福|ふく}→祝福：13733_shukufuku⟧: blessing, benediction\n\nUSAGE:\n⟦お{祝|いわ}い→お祝い：01339_oiwai⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{言|い}う→言う：00515_iu⟧ means to offer congratulations. お{祝|いわ}い can also refer to the gift or money given on a celebratory occasion.",
